{"chunk_id": "c27863562469", "text": "Kumbhakarna, the gigantic brother of Ravana, storms the battlefield and devastates the monkey army with terrifying strength. He crushes, devours, and scatters thousands of warriors, resisting attacks from champions like Hanuman, Nila, and Angada. Sugriva confronts him but is struck down and carried toward Lanka as a captive, though he later regains consciousness and mutilates the titan\u2019s ears and nose before escaping back to Rama. Enraged and blood\u2011soaked, Kumbhakarna returns to battle and continues slaughtering friend and foe alike in his frenzy. Lakshmana challenges him but directs the fight toward Rama. In a climactic duel, Rama methodically disarms the titan\u2014severing his arms, then his legs\u2014before finally loosing a divine arrow that decapitates him. The fall of Kumbhakarna shakes the world and brings jubilation to the gods, marking a decisive turning point in the war for Lanka.\nKumbhakarna devastates the monkey army, wounds many heroes, but Rama ultimately dismembers and kills the gigantic titan in a climactic battle.\nThemes: heroic battle, monstrous power, sacrifice and courage, divine weapons, fall of a titan", "vector": [-0.0005713221034966409, -0.03156771510839462, 0.016246533021330833, 0.006384927313774824, -0.0064873769879341125, 0.02897673100233078, -0.02323954924941063, -0.008936254307627678, -0.023279206827282906, -0.03014002926647663, 0.01007311511784792, 0.015849953517317772, 0.021269870921969414, 0.00307514239102602, 0.0006258517387323081, -0.005819801706820726, 0.04338578134775162, -0.012703757733106613, 0.02550005167722702, -0.033841438591480255, 0.008103437721729279, 0.00022369553335011005, -0.010251576080918312, 0.006064359098672867, -0.037754353135824203, 0.024640796706080437, 0.02072788029909134, -0.04063616320490837, 0.019035808742046356, -0.0059685190208256245, -0.009775680489838123, -0.01133555918931961, -0.0019019284518435597, 0.00400545122101903, -0.03225512057542801, 0.0009030441